text I place my hand on Nagisa's head, and stroke her hair gently.
text I hear the announcer's voice coming from the TV in a low volume, reporting on the situation.
text The bus had gone into a service area and stopped.
text I can see several nurses in doctor's robes running up there from the edge of the screen.
text The front door of the bus opens.
text ...My eyes open wide.
text Elderly people descend out from inside the bus.
text Many passengers were getting off the bus there.
text All of them women, children, and the elderly.
text The door of the bus then closes.
text And it drives off again.
text I can hear a sigh of relief coming from Nagisa.
text Before I realize it, I'm holding Nagisa's shoulders.
music ~
text In my mind, I'd thought it would just be too big a coincidence.
text But I wonder why.
text Maybe Nagisa's worries have transferred over to me.
music BGM01.mp3
text For some reason... I couldn't help but feel he was "there."
text Suddenly the phone rings, and Nagisa and I exchange glances.
