text Then, the next service area.
text The bus remained at a stop.
text The person who appears from the opened door...
text ...is a man of familiar stature.
text It's the figure of the man holding a cigarette in his mouth, always looking as if he's about to complain about something.
text However, he's slouching more than normal, and he leans his weight onto the body of the bus, looking as if he's in pain.
text I can't quite see his wound because he's wearing a black top, but his jeans are stained with blood, like someone spilled black paint all over them.
text He faces the police while keeping a distance from them, while the bus driver is still being held hostage inside the bus.
text He has some kind of exchange with them, but it's too far away, so I can't quite tell what is happening.
text I wonder if they're not allowed to show his face on TV in this sort of situation.
text The police carry a megaphone (or at least I think it is) to the bus, and throw it toward it.
text The injured man picks it up slowly.
text He checks to see whether it's turned on, and then starts shouting something.
text It isn't quite audible.
text The man looks satisfied, and gets on the bus once again.
text Descending from the bus in his stead... is the bus driver, wearing his uniform.
text The moment the driver gets down onto the ground, the door closes, and the bus departs.
text The tires slip as the bus makes a large U-turn, and it leaves the service area behind.
text Police cars and ambulances immediately follow after it.
text The only ones left inside... are the young man and the injured man.
text So he's the one driving the bus right now?
text Just what is that guy trying to do?
text We all hold our breath, and carefully watch over the proceedings.
text @[Tomoya]
text ...
text After a few moments, a videotape recording is played back.
text With the audio corrected, you could now hear what he had been saying.
music ~
text ──"We're going to be setting out on a trip now!"
text I can hear him.
text ──"We've actually clicked with each other!"
text ──"We've become friends!"
text ──"The boy has someone he wants to see!"
text ──"His grandmother who raised him when he was little!"
text ──"He says she'd been bedridden ever since 5 years ago!"
text ──"He doesn't know how she's doing right now..."
text ──"But despite that, he's going to come see her!"
text ──"And when he checks to find out how she's doing, I'm going to make sure I'm next to him so he can get through it!"
text ──"All right?! You understand?!"
jump SEEN7200_1_0.scr
